# Accessibility and RTL Rules

## Keyboard and Focus
- All interactive elements MUST be keyboard reachable and operable.
- Visible focus state MUST exist (`focus-visible` styling) for every interactive control.
- Dialogs, popovers, and menus MUST support Escape and proper focus return.

## Semantic and Screen Reader Requirements
- Inputs MUST be associated with labels.
- Icon-only controls MUST include `aria-label`.
- Tables MUST include semantic headers and understandable column labels.
- Status/error/success updates SHOULD be announced via live regions where applicable.

## Contrast and Information Clarity
- Text MUST meet WCAG AA minimum contrast expectations.
- State MUST NOT be conveyed by color alone; include text or icon cues.
- Required fields MUST be clearly indicated and described in accessible terms.

## RTL Readiness
- Prefer logical direction utilities and start/end alignment over left/right hardcoding.
- Directional icons SHOULD be reviewed for RTL flipping behavior.

## Definition of Done for Accessibility
1. Keyboard path tested for modified interactions
2. No missing labels for newly added controls
3. Focus visibility confirmed
4. RTL-sensitive spacing/alignment considered
